    {
      "seq": 35,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "concepts",
      "local_id": "SBJ003",
      "dda_id": "DMC000000110",
      "fields": {
        "concept_description": "There is one of these for each classification applied to a legal entity. In this structure it names what a vehicle is for: management company, holding company, special purpose vehicle, tax blocker, fund vehicle or operating company. If you need to know which vehicles in a structure are tax blockers, this is what you go by. It is not a statement of what a body is to another, which comes from relationships.",
        "concept_parent_rel": "ONE_TO_MANY_OPTIONAL"
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 36,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "concepts",
      "local_id": "SBJ007",
      "dda_id": "DMC000000128",
      "fields": {
        "concept_description": "There is one of these for each price of an instrument as at a date and of a given price type. In this structure it holds the fair value per unit of a private holding, with its level in the fair value hierarchy. If you need to value any fund's holding of an instrument, multiply the units it holds by this. It is not the amount a fund paid, which is held on the transaction.",
        "concept_parent_rel": "ONE_TO_MANY_OPTIONAL"
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 37,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "concepts",
      "local_id": "SBJ009",
      "dda_id": "DMC000000030",
      "fields": {
        "concept_description": "There is one of these for each valuation of a legal entity as at a date and on a named measure of value. In this structure it holds the net asset value of a fund and the equity value or enterprise value of a portfolio company or vehicle. If you need the value of a fund or a company at a reporting date, this is what you go by. A new valuation does not replace an earlier one, because each is kept for its own date. It is a view taken on a date and not a movement of money, so it is not a transaction. It is the value of the whole body and not the value of one fund's holding in it, which is the price per unit multiplied by the units held, and it is not the fair value of a single instrument, which is held with the instrument's price.",
        "concept_parent_rel": null
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 38,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "concepts",
      "local_id": "SBJ010",
      "dda_id": "DMC000000032",
      "fields": {
        "concept_description": "There is one of these for each movement of money or of a holding within a transaction, for one party and one purpose. If you need to know who paid or received what, in which currency, for which instrument and how many units, and when it settled, this is what you go by. A capital call has one leg for each investor. It is not the transaction itself, which holds what the event was and when it took place.",
        "concept_parent_rel": "ONE_TO_MANY_OPTIONAL"
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 39,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "relationships",
      "local_id": "REL001",
      "dda_id": "DMR000000001",
      "fields": {
        "relationship_code": "LegalEntityFundManagedBy",
        "relationship_description": "A fund is managed by a general partner or manager for as long as the arrangement lasts, and a fund has one manager at a time, so the periods of its managers do not overlap. It holds nothing about the fund itself: the facts of the fund, such as its vintage year, strategy, currency and domicile, stay with the fund when its manager is replaced. It is not the fund's limited partners, who are linked by commitments.",
        "relationship_forward_verb": "Is Managed By",
        "relationship_inverse_verb": "Manages",
        "relationship_source_role": "Fund",
        "relationship_target_role": "GP",
        "relationship_source_role_plural": "Funds",
        "relationship_target_role_plural": "GPs",
        "relationship_cardinality": "MANY_TO_ONE",
        "relationship_dates": true,
        "relationship_domain": "DMD000000012",
        "relationship_destination_domain": "DMD000000012"
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 40,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "relationships",
      "local_id": "REL002",
      "dda_id": "DMR000000004",
      "fields": {
        "relationship_code": "LegalEntityFundLPCommitment",
        "relationship_description": "A limited partner has committed capital to a fund for as long as the commitment runs. A limited partner may commit to several funds and a fund has many limited partners, and a second purchase of an existing interest is a further commitment of its own type. The amount, type and status belong to the commitment. It is not the money called or paid out, which is recorded as transactions.",
        "relationship_forward_verb": "Commits To",
        "relationship_inverse_verb": "Receives Commitment From",
        "relationship_source_role": "LP",
        "relationship_target_role": "Fund",
        "relationship_source_role_plural": "LPs",
        "relationship_target_role_plural": "Funds",
        "relationship_cardinality": "MANY_TO_MANY",
        "relationship_dates": true,
        "relationship_domain": "DMD000000012",
        "relationship_destination_domain": "DMD000000012"
      },
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "seq": 41,
      "op": "update",
      "entity": "relationships",
      "local_id": "REL003",
      "dda_id": "DMR000000002",
      "fields": {
        "relationship_code": "LegalEntityPEInvestor",
        "relationship_description": "A fund or vehicle holds a stake in a portfolio company or a holding vehicle for as long as it holds it. Several investors may hold one company and one investor may hold several. The economic share, voting share and control type belong to the stake. It is not what was paid for the stake, which is recorded as transactions.",
        "relationship_forward_verb": "Receives Investment From",
        "relationship_inverse_verb": "Invests In",
        "relationship_source_role": "PortCo",
